| `scripts/scan_secrets.py` | The gitleaks adapter, and the one home of the scanner record: `write_record` writes the program's path, rev and sha256 to `secrets.scanner.record_file`, `record_is_ignored` says whether git would commit that file, and every scan runs only a program that matches the record; `scripts/install_scanner.py` imports those helpers, so the installer and the scan read one record by one rule. | `make secret-scan`; the commit hook | [`secrets.scanner.record_file`](settings.md#configprojectjson), [`secrets.scanner.rev`](settings.md#configprojectjson) | Never runs a scanner found on PATH, and fetches nothing: `make secrets-install` does. Not the keyed gate: `tests/integration/test_committed_secrets_gate.py` judges names. write_record raises PathEscape for a record escaping the project before any mutation; the CLI reports CONFIG. Checks judge paths at call time; a link swapped before the write is not caught. | [deterministic-checks.md](../guides/deterministic-checks.md) | always |
